# entrypoint.sh gets COPY'd straight into the Docker image and run via
# /bin/sh -- CRLF line endings there break it outright ("/bin/sh^M: bad
# interpreter" or similar), which core.autocrlf=true (the common Windows
# Git default) would otherwise introduce on checkout despite the repo's
# own blob staying LF. Force LF for every .sh file regardless of the
# checking-out machine's autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
